    {"id": "_github_workflows_release_runtime_repair_legacy_no_installer", "label": "No-installer constraint (legacy Qt builder removed)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.github\\workflows\\release-runtime-repair.yml", "source_location": "comment header", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This workflow historically ran the legacy Qt PyInstaller/Inno Setup builder and uploaded its output under the desktop asset names, making the published Setup.exe ambiguous. It now deliberately omits Inno Setup entirely, builds only a no-installer onedir, and fails the run if any desktop installer artifact appears, so runtime-repair releases can never masquerade as the desktop app."}
